examples.question_text:
Use the graph to find (a) the amount borrowed and (b) the amount still owing after $75$ months, estimated to the nearest $\$5000$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=105,ymin=0,ymax=98000,xtick={0,25,50,75,100},ytick={0,15000,30000,45000,60000,75000,90000},grid=both,grid style={color=housegrid,line width=0.25pt},samples=80,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,tick style={black},ticklabel style={text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,/pgf/number format/fixed},label style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},xlabel={Months},ylabel={Balance owing (\$)},ylabel style={at={(axis description cs:-0.37,0.5)},anchor=south}]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:100]{90000*(2-exp(x*0.00693147180559945))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
(a) At month $0$, the balance is $\$90\,000$, so that is the amount borrowed.
(b) Read up from $75$ months to the curve, then across to the value axis. The balance is a little below $\$30\,000$, so the estimate to the nearest $\$5000$ is $\$30\,000$. The curve falls more steeply later; it is not a straight-line decrease.
